The indigenous population hasn't changed at all - they are still in need of the same appreponation, as before.
Over time, when the new population is starting to adapt to their new environment, they begin to look less and less similar to the other population.
Eventually, after a thousand or even millions of years, these two populations will look so different that they can not be called the same species.
